 they are  transferred to the  vacuum region of mass spec so in the  first vacuum region of  ms it isolates the  pesticides parent iron at fixed mass  these parent ions undergo further  fragmentation  in the collagen cell to form unique  product ions  and in the last part of the ms  it isolates and detects one of the  product ions  at the fixed mass so the matrix  interference can happen  when a hemp matrix compound has the same  elusion time parent time and product  iron as your pesticide  so in this next slide essentially i'm  trying to show here is that  if i try to use a conventional  m mass transitions for propynchronozole  uh in hemp what we see here in the top  part of the slide is that  we cannot differentiate between the  signal from a  hemp matrix and from a hemp matrix spike  with 100 ppp  so therefore it is very difficult to  meet california actual limits of 100 ppb  for this compound in hemp  but if i look at the bottom part of the  slide  and in which basically we are using  much more optimized mass transitions for  this pesticide propaganda result  we can minimize the matrix interference  signal which  is the net rays and now we can easily  meet  uh the california actual limits of 100  ppb  for this compound in hemp matrix  due to no matrix interface  next i would like to talk about the  sample preparation methods we can use  for extraction of pesticides from hemp  matrix so we could have used uh  any of these four sample preparation  methods  if you used quechu's dispersive solid  phase extraction and solid extraction  you will find that these methods are  very slow  difficult expensive and also show  poor recoveries for some of the  pesticide compounds  in comparison to these three sample  preparation techniques  sovereign extraction is fast quick  cheap and shows good recovery for  all the compounds therefore we believe  that solvent extraction is the best  sample  preparation method to achieve high  throughput in cannabis and hemp testing  labs for pesticide analysis  before i show you the  sample preparation recovery data  i would like to describe you  the formula for the sample preparation  recovery  it's essentially can be calculated by  taking a ratio  of the signal for an analyte in the  pre-spike extract  to the analyte signal in the post file  extract  in this slide the table shows excellent  recovery  for all the pesticides using  acetonitrile extraction  we get recoveries for all the pesticides  in the range of  80 to 120 percent with rst  less than 10  for comparison if we use sweatshirts  the recovery for demerizade would be low  since demonozite is a very polar  compound it has a very low  optimal water partition coefficient of  minus 1.5  therefore it will stay in the water  phase  during the salting out step of the  questions  if you used dispersive solid phase  extraction  or solid food extraction you would find  that  recovery for few more pesticides such as  pinocyte and few more  would be low lower than the acceptable  range of 80 to 120 percent  as i mentioned earlier a hemp matrix is  very  challenging and therefore we observed  ion separation for the signal of a  number of pesticides  in hemp matrix  a layman term ion separation means that  the  when the signal for your analyte in  sample is  uh less than uh the signal in your  solvent by 20  or more iron enhancement is observed  when the signal for your analyte in  sample  is greater than uh then the signal is  solvent by  20 or more for the most  analytes we observed ion suppression  from hemp matrix  for very few analytes we see ion  enhancement  and therefore during the rest of our  talk i would only  focus on ion separation effects from the  matrix at this stage  i would like to introduce another term  which is called overall recovery overall  recovery  depends both on your sample  preparation recovery and ion suppression  effects  so in this formula the first ratio  represents  the sample preparation recovery and the  second  ratio