r by  standard deviation of all the data if  the z-scores  are less than 2 that means your results  are satisfactory  and you pass the test if your z-scores  are between  2 and 3 that means your results are  questionable and you just pass the test  if your z-scores are greater than three  that means  your results are not acceptable and you  did not pass the test  and now you need to go back to the  drawing board and  determine ways to improve the  performance of your method  so we participated in emerald  scientific proficiency test for  66 pesticides in hemp and  i'm pleased to inform everyone that we  pass  this test with flying colors since  all the z-scores for  our method were less than two with no  false  positives and no false negatives and  also if you look at the z-score  distribution  with our method about 92  of the z-scores were less than 1.  this showed further that our method is  quite accurate for quantification of  66 pesticides in hand  in next three slides i would just like  to show you that  we can easily meet all the california  action limits for the pesticides in hemp  some of these pesticides are analyzed by  gcms ms  traditionally but we can analyze using  these pesticides using our novel method  with esi and apci iron source  and if you look at the last column of  this table  it shows you the ratio of the action  limits  to our to our method loq  so this number is greater than 2  this shows  quite clearly that we can easily meet  california action limits for  all the 66 pesticides in hemp  the second slide for this  set of three slides shows you again that  we can meet  california actual limits for these  pesticides in hand  and in this slide we are showing the  action limits for category one  pesticides in hand  and our method loq  so the main advantage of our of our  method is that now the customers only  need to use  one instrument one scientist  and one set of consumables to analyze  all the pesticides on california list in  hand  with th